name: Bounded history preserves exact investigation access and explains damaged records
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI || READY THE MAP RUN | ready
submit: campaign
require-live-snap: 25 History partial | bounded-history
expect-not: no campaigns planned
ask: Does the history browser disclose its bounded result and incomplete spending without claiming that it lists the whole workspace?
paste-file: @ART/history-exact-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 held-1 | exact-investigation
expect: held-2
nav-mode:
keys: Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 held-2 | selected-recorded-job
expect: 0 total attempts
keys: r
require-live-snap: 20 held-2 | exact-identity-after-refresh
ask: Can an operator open the requested investigation beyond the browse limit, inspect its exact recorded job and refresh without changing identity or starting work?
resize: 160x48
keys: Home
live-snap: history-detail-160x48
expect: History partial
resize: 96x89
keys: Home
live-snap: history-detail-96x89
expect: History partial
resize: 80x24
keys: Home
live-snap: history-detail-80x24
expect: History partial
resize: 60x20
keys: Home
live-snap: history-detail-60x20
expect: History partial
resize: 40x12
keys: Home
live-snap: history-detail-40x12
expect: History partial
keys: NPage
live-snap: history-read-page-1
keys: NPage
live-snap: history-read-page-2
keys: NPage
live-snap: history-read-page-3
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART paging
ask: Are partial history, the selected job and its inspection/back controls readable by paging across the six viewport sizes?
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART damage
keys: r Home
require-live-snap: 25 1 unreadable, 1 symlink(s) skipped | damaged-history
expect: held-2
expect-not: limit of 100 investigations reached
expect-not: no campaigns planned
ask: Does damaged history preserve the readable selected investigation and disclose unreadable records and skipped symlinks without treating missing cost as zero?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART block
keys: r Home
require-live-snap: 25 History unavailable | directory-unavailable
expect-not: no campaigns planned
resize: 40x12
keys: Home
live-snap: directory-unavailable-40x12
keys: End
live-snap: directory-recovery-controls-40x12
ask: Does a blocked history directory produce an honest unavailable state with a recovery action instead of a successful empty workspace?
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restore
keys: r
require-live-snap: 25 History partial | restored-history
paste-file: @ART/history-exact-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 held-1 | recovered-investigation
expect: held-2
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/campaign_history.py @TMP_TARGET @ART verify
ask: After explicit repair and refresh, can the operator inspect the same untouched plan without new queues, reservations, findings or model requests?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
